# Per-sample admixture

**What this is.** The classic ADMIXTURE-style overview: every
sample in the cohort as one vertical strip, sorted by primary
FLARE ancestry → descending proportion within group. Each sample's
FLARE component vector is summed by the RF label its components
map to under `merged_groups_rf.tsv`, so colors are SP6 ancestries
(faithful to the bundle's mapping — when the collector emits
`afr.3` we honour it the same as `afr`).

**How to read this chart.** Long single-color runs at the left
edge are "pure" samples; the middle of each color band shows
admixed individuals (multiple colors stacked at non-trivial
heights). Cohort-wide proportions appear as the relative widths
of each color block. If you want per-cluster decomposition see
the cohort composition section.

